{
    "_comment": "Maps a unit name key to the art that draws it. A key can be: an exact tiered name ('Medium Tank III'), an era range ('Infantry 1900-1925'), or a bare family name used as the catch-all for every tier/year that has no more specific entry ('Infantry', 'Artillery'). Anything not covered here falls back to the classic art.",
    "_comment_variants": "A key's value is either one entry or a list of them. Each entry is either a plain filename (applies to whichever country asks) or an object {'file': ..., 'countries': [...]} restricted to those country ids -- the exact strings that key data/json/countries_data.json, e.g. 'Germany', 'German Reich', 'German Empire'. A country matching one of the restricted entries sees that picture; everyone else falls through to the first unrestricted entry for that key, and if there isn't one, to the next fallback rule (e.g. 'Infantry 1900-1925' missing a generic falls back to the bare 'Infantry' entry below) and eventually to classic. See map_logic/rendering/symbol_loader.py for the exact matching and fallback rules.",
    "_comment_cultures": "Culture groups allow reusing common country sets. In a 'countries' field, use either a culture group name (string) or a list of country ids (array). Example: 'countries': 'germanic' or 'countries': ['Germany', 'France'].",
    "_comment_folders": "'file' paths are relative to this style's folder and may include a subfolder -- images here are organized into one subfolder per culture group (e.g. 'french/Char_B1_bis.png') purely for tidiness; the loader just joins the path, so the subfolder name has no effect on which countries see the art. Infantry filenames drop their culture prefix (e.g. 'infantry_1914.png' rather than 'french_infantry_1914.png') since the subfolder already says which culture it is.",
    "_cultures": {
        "germanic": ["Germany", "German Reich", "German Empire", "Weimar Republic"],
        "austrian": ["Austria-Hungary", "Austria"],
        "russian": ["Russia", "Soviet Union"],
        "british": ["United Kingdom", "England", "Union of Britain"],
        "french": ["France", "Commune of France", "National France", "Vichy France", "Free France"],
        "italian": ["Italy", "Socialist Republic of Italy"],
        "american": ["United States of America"]
    },

